# CE-EP-001 — Audience Engagement Phase 1 Implementation

## Status

Approved for Implementation

---

# Purpose

Implement the first Audience Engagement capability for Bible Therapy Assistant (BTA).

This implementation establishes the reusable Audience Engagement platform capability while temporarily residing within the BibleSearchSite repository.

The implementation provides a complete end-to-end workflow from the BTA user interface through HubSpot CRM while intentionally remaining independent of future PostgreSQL, Identity, Marketing Automation, and additional TAD Concepts domains.

---

# Scope

Included

- Audience Engagement frontend component
- Backend Engagement Route
- Backend Engagement Service
- HubSpot CRM integration
- Client-side validation
- Backend validation
- Success confirmation
- End-to-end testing

Excluded

- PostgreSQL
- CRM replacement abstraction
- Identity
- Authentication
- Authorization
- Marketing automation
- ETL
- Stripe
- User Accounts
- Analytics

---

# Architectural Principle

Audience Engagement is a Platform Interaction Capability.

Although implemented inside the BibleSearchSite repository, it is architecturally owned by the future TAD Concepts orchestration platform.

Its implementation shall remain loosely coupled to enable future extraction with minimal refactoring.

---

# Architectural Pattern

Audience Engagement shall follow the same interaction pattern established by the existing Donation capability.

Presentation

↓

Backend Route

↓

Business Service

↓

External Provider

↓

HubSpot CRM

Implementation shall follow the architectural structure only.

No Donation business logic shall be reused.

